        game and refreshed within 48 hours of each version patch.” Every snapshot is cross-checked against
        <a href="https://genshin.hoyoverse.com" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="text-forest-600 underline underline-offset-4">HoYoverse’s official Genshin Impact site</a>
        and the community-maintained
        <a href="https://genshin-impact.fandom.com/wiki/Genshin_Impact_Wiki" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="text-forest-600 underline underline-offset-4">Genshin Impact Wiki</a>;
        patch timing follows announcements on the
        <a href="https://www.youtube.com/@GenshinImpact" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="text-forest-600 underline underline-offset-4">official Genshin Impact YouTube channel</a>.
      </p>
      <blockquote class="mt-4 border-l-4 border-forest-500 pl-4">
        <p class="text-sm leading-relaxed text-[var(--muted)]">
          “When characters or enemies attack their targets, they deal damage (abbreviated as DMG) based on their own
          and their target’s attributes. … There are eight damage types: seven Elemental and one Physical.”
        </p>
        <cite class="mt-2 block text-xs not-italic text-[var(--text)]">
          — <a href="https://genshin-impact.fandom.com/wiki/Damage" target="_blank" rel="noopener"
          class="text-forest-600 underline underline-offset-4">Genshin Impact Wiki</a>, “Damage”, section “Damage”
        </cite>
      </blockquote>
    </div>

    <div class="panel mt-6 flex flex-col gap-5 p-6 sm:flex-row sm:items-start">
      <span class="flex h-16 w-16 shrink-0 items-center justify-center rounded-2xl bg-forest-500/12 text-2xl font-semibold text-forest-600 ring-1 ring-forest-500/25" aria-hidden="true">K</span>
      <div>
        <p class="text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-[0.18em] text-forest-600">Maintained by</p>
        <p class="mt-1 text-lg font-semibold text-[var(--text)]">Kai Ren</p>
        <p class="mt-1 text-sm leading-relaxed text-[var(--muted)]">
          Independent developer and long-time Genshin Impact player. Maintains the character and weapon data against the live game,
